<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">US oil embargo against Japan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as oil embargo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The US oil embargo against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> was the cutting off of American oil exports to Japan in 1941, imposed in response to Japanese expansion in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> note that Japan imported approximately eighty percent of its oil from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The embargo therefore presented a direct threat to Japan's war effort and strategically drove the decision to attack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attack-on-pearl-harbor">Pearl Harbor</a>.</p></div>
